# Next.js App Router — ARTSA Frontend

Source: [awesome-cursorrules/rules/nextjs.mdc](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules)

## Structure
- App Router under `frontend/app/`; shared UI in `frontend/components/`; utilities in `frontend/lib/`
- Route-specific components colocate in `app/<route>/`; reusable pieces in `components/ui`, `components/layout`, `components/shared`
- Use lowercase-with-dashes for multi-word directories (e.g. `components/attack-library`)

## Server vs Client
- Default to Server Components; add `'use client'` only for hooks, browser APIs, or event handlers
- Keep client boundaries small; wrap async client trees in `Suspense` with skeleton fallbacks
- Prefer server fetching in RSC; use existing `fetchFromBackend()` in client pages when WebSocket or polling is required

## Performance
- Dynamic `import()` for heavy charts (Recharts, D3 topology) and modals
- Minimize `useEffect` for data that can be fetched on the server or via SWR-style polling
- Use `next/image` for static assets; lazy-load below-the-fold dashboard panels

## Routing & UX
- Every route gets consistent loading via shared skeleton components
- Use `error.tsx` boundaries for API failures; show actionable retry UI for containment API outages
- Preserve existing API paths (`/api/v1/*`) — do not change backend contracts from the frontend

## Forms
- Validate with Zod at boundaries; show inline field errors
- Disable submit while loading; preserve WCAG focus management on success/error
